body:
@thinkingmedia We are not talking about nullish/falsey values and their differences, but if it is OK in general to completely remove the maxLimit functionality. So far you HAD to set a value >= 1 for security reasons. Allowing 0 (or anything else < 1) would overwrite the security feature here, so that's why I am hesistent to just "agree".

@EOM I agree we need to fix the warning one way or another :) The other way would be to throw a clear exception "Please set a valid maxLimit value >= 1".

Just to be clear:
The security feature is to prevent DDOS via ?limit=99999999999 etc if your table ever got enough records and kill it this way.
Manually setting it to a high value yourself is your own very explicit "doing" then, whereas if the framework makes 0 => disable possible this kind of cloaks the issue a bit more.
